3. NON-DISCRIMINATION & INVARIANT ENFORCEMENT
Any deployment, modification, or derivative work of this Software executing in a live operational, public, or sovereign environment must strictly uphold the following Kernel Invariants:
   a. Sector Non-Discrimination: Micro-collection rate derivatives (∂C_i / ∂V_i) must apply uniformly across all economic sectors without entity-level, corporate tax-ID, or political exemptions.
   b. Damped Decay & Slew-Rate Limits: Rate-of-change parameters (|dλ/dt|) must remain strictly bounded by compiled saturation limiters to prevent sudden step-function policy shocks.
   c. Autonomous Safety Floor: The system must execute local emergency freeze protocols (λ -> 0) whenever regional aggregate demand (D_r) drops below critical survival thresholds (D_critical).

4. OPEN TELEMETRY & AUDITABILITY
Any public or sovereign deployment must maintain open verification endpoints. All state adjustments, parameter updates, and telemetry ingests must provide Zero-Knowledge (ZK) or cryptographically verifiable execution proofs accessible to public inspection.

